matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","abstract":[{"text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing. The card maps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Position to its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch’s rubber-band bounds, and pulses Reset when both position axes are within the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"placed graph’s 100-point center tolerance.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}]}}}